From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Subject: [PATCH] status/keyboard: no reload on password focus without IBus sources

Focusing a password field disables IBus input sources and focusing
anything else enables them again, each through reload(): the keymap is
reapplied and sources-changed rebuilds the screen keyboard. With only XKB
sources there is nothing to disable, yet every focus change between a
password and another field still reloaded. On a phone lock screen, where
the password field takes and gives up focus as it slides in and out, each
reload held the main thread for 30-70 ms, several times per swipe.

--- a/js/ui/status/keyboard.js
+++ b/js/ui/status/keyboard.js
@@ -725,6 +725,11 @@ export class InputSourceManager extends Signals.EventEmitter {
         // the focus change caused by the switcher popup causing this purpose change.
         if (this._switcherPopup)
             return;
+        // Without IBus sources a password field has nothing to switch off,
+        // and a reload would rebuild the keymap and the screen keyboard.
+        if (!this._disableIBus &&
+            !this._settings.inputSources.some(s => s.type === INPUT_SOURCE_TYPE_IBUS))
+            return;
         if (purpose === IBus.InputPurpose.PASSWORD) {
             if (Object.keys(this._inputSources).length === Object.keys(this._ibusSources).length)
                 return;
